    "# Project Phase 1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "449af346-c017-4ff3-af35-7a244ccad4d5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "In the city of Boston Public Transportation has come very far but there are always more ways to improve. I Plan to use public data from the city of Boston and the MBTA to analyze which areas are faster at walking and which are faster on the MBTA. With this data I will compare it to the census data in the area and show which underrepresented areas are targeted by poor public transport managing and are left out of the public transport circles in the city. Certain areas also lack proper access to the T and are serviced only by bus route. We want to investigate the differences in reliability between T and bus public transit travel."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d5706a16-0d05-4db5-9a7c-b34b00fb9e7d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import requests\n",
    "\n",
    "mbta = requests.get(\"https://api-v3.mbta.com/stops?filter[latitude]=42.3555&filter[longitude]=-71.0603&filter[radius]=0.02\").json()\n",
    "print(\"MBTA:\", list(mbta[\"data\"][0][\"attributes\"].keys()))\n",
    "reliability_mbta_api = requests.get(
    "https://api-v3.mbta.com/predictions",
    params={"filter[route]": "Red", "page[limit]": 200000})\n",
    "\n",
    "census = requests.get(\"https://api.census.gov/data/2022/acs/acs5?get=NAME,B19013_001E,B08201_001E,B08201_002E,B03002_001E,B03002_003E&for=tract:*&in=state:25%20county:025\").json()\n",
    "print(\"Census:\", census[0])\n",
    "\n",
    "//cant be ran without this unfortunately\n",
    "key = \n",
    "walk = requests.post(\"https://api.openrouteservice.org/v2/directions/foot-walking/json\", headers={\"Authorization\": key}, json={\"coordinates\": [[-71.0603, 42.3555], [-71.0552, 42.3523]]}).json()\n",
    "print(\"Walking:\", list(walk[\"routes\"][0][\"summary\"].keys()))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d7bca75b-a44e-4f21-b5d3-2486af86e6ae",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "I plan to use categories like stop names and their locations (route information) to better purpose the data to make it fully useable and compare it to walking distances within the same latitude and longitudes using the openrouteservie api. Using this data I will compare it to the census data to better highlight which areas are being underrepresented and where the social statuses in the area stand to better identify insights in the area. Additionally we will look at zip codes of MBTA stops and their respective aggregate delays/reliability and cross reference that with census data for socioeconomic factors such as average income."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "821f9188-9a16-413c-aa57-ccf0b3a5bfa8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The MBTA data will provide information about the location and availability of public transportation stops and routes, while Census data will provide information about the population, income, vehicle availability, and demographics of each area. Walking-route data will allow us to calculate how long it takes to travel between locations by foot, which can then be compared with travel times using the MBTA. Specifically I will look at factors such as median income, racial demographics, vehicle availability, number of nearby MBTA stops, and travel times. This will allow us to identify communities where certain demographic or socioeconomic groups have fewer transportation options or significantly longer transit times or much more varied public transit reliability than other areas of Boston. I plan to find how the ratio of walking times and MBTA times change based on certain locations on different backgrounds."
   ]
  }
